sentences.l:
she then
on the mainland ran aground, as far as up to a half of the whole of her,
hurrying;

And these things then beside the trunk of the olive all together they put,
out of the road, lest in some way some one of wayfaring men,
before Odysseus woke, coming upon them should do them harm;

and near her came the earth-shaker,
who her into a stone made and rooted her beneath,
striking with a downturned hand;

But he woke, heavenly Odysseus,
sleeping in his father’s land, and did not know it,
already long absent;

for around him the goddess poured a mist,
Pallas Athena, daughter of Zeus, so that him himself
she might make unknown, and tell each thing,
